  "pr_title": "build(tooling): license spsync under MIT",
  "pr_description": "## Goal\n\nLicense spsync under MIT and prepare the repository to become public, so teammates can install spsync without a GitHub account or token.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe repository now has a `LICENSE` file with the MIT license text. `pyproject.toml` declares `license = \"MIT\"` and lists the file in `license-files`, so the source package and the wheel both include it.\n\nThe vendored anti-slop Oxlint rules in `obsidian-plugin/tools/oxlint/anti-slop/` had no license file of their own. The upstream MIT `LICENSE` from the vendored revision is now copied unchanged into that directory. The vendored ESLint Stylistic code keeps its existing MIT `LICENSE`. `UPSTREAM.md` records both license files.\n\nThe README has three new sections for a public project. Contributing says that issues are welcome and that the project does not accept pull requests from outside the team. Maintainers names the maintainer. License states the MIT license and names `merge3` as a GPL-2.0-or-later dependency that the repository declares but does not include.\n\nA gitleaks scan of the full history found one item. The item is in `.pi/fabric/mesh/state.json` from commit `98cb46e`, a pi session-state file that a later commit removed from git. The flagged value is a state key, `topology/participants/` followed by a SHA-256 participant hash, not a credential. `.gitleaksignore` lists that one fingerprint and explains why.\n\nThis change does not touch docx reading or patching.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `uv run pytest`: 41 passed.\n- `uv lock --check`: the lockfile is current.\n- `uv build`: the source package and the wheel both contain `LICENSE`.\n- `gitleaks git --log-opts=\"--all\" --redact .` with gitleaks 8.30.1: 46 commits scanned, no leaks found.\n- The pre-commit hook ran for each commit. The changed files have no em-dashes and no curly quotation marks.\n\nAfter this PR merges, the repository becomes public with `gh repo edit jekozyra/spsync --visibility public --accept-visibility-change-consequences`. `gh repo view jekozyra/spsync --json visibility` must then return `PUBLIC`.\n\n## Issue\n\nCloses #7\n"
}